			"widgets_values":[
				"A vertical, cinematic nighttime photograph shows a traditional Chinese waterside street rendered in highly detailed realistic style. Near the upper portion of the image, a large luminous full moon glows in the deep navy-blue sky slightly left of center, surrounded by soft atmospheric haze and faint clouds. Dark, layered rooftops with curved tile ridgelines stretch diagonally from both sides, framing the narrow old-town passage. Warm lanterns mounted along the timber-and-stone buildings emit amber-yellow light, contrasting strongly with the cool blue moonlight. In the far background, weathered stone architecture, arched openings, stacked eaves, and wet-looking surfaces appear partially obscured by shallow-depth-of-field blur, giving the scene an antique, misty quality.\n\nAcross the middle-left and lower-left areas, several out-of-focus human figures move through the street. They wear muted gray-brown robes or long garments resembling historical attire, though their bodies are heavily motion-blurred and secondary to the main figure. Wooden balcony posts and railings line the canal side, including cylindrical turned balusters with rounded finials, all made of aged brown wood with glossy highlights from moisture and lamplight. A narrow waterway occupies much of the left and central background, reflecting blue-white moonlight and gold lantern tones in rippled bands.\n\nDominating the center and lower half of the composition is a young adult East Asian woman shown in intimate close-up from a low, selfie-like angle. She has fair, smooth skin, an oval face, refined cheekbones, expressive almond-shaped brown eyes, neatly groomed brows, defined eyelashes, subtle eyeliner, soft peach-pink eyeshadow, delicate blush, and muted rose-red lipstick with satin sheen. Her expression is calm, focused, and slightly serious as she looks directly into the camera. Loose dark brown-black hair frames her forehead and cheeks, with wispy bangs catching backlight, while the rest of her hair is styled back in an elegant updo decorated with translucent white flower ornaments, dangling beads, pearls, and metallic pins. Small dangling earrings are partly visible beneath her hair.\n\nShe wears flowing moon-white or cream-white silk-satin Hanfu-inspired clothing with embroidered blossoms and branching vines along the collar, chest panel, sleeve edges, and bodice. The material appears silky and lightweight, forming broad draped sleeves and folded layers over her torso. Gold-toned closures run vertically near the neckline, adding fine ornamental detail. Her posture leans forward over a rustic stone bridge or riverside ledge, bringing her hands very close to the viewer and creating strong foreshortening. One forearm extends from the center toward the lower-right area, lit warmly by candlelike reflection, while the wide sleeve expands around the wrist in soft pleated fabric.\n\nIn the foreground, centered near the bottom, the woman presents a complete polished celadon-green porcelain teapoint with embossed botanical relief pattern covering the rounded body, domed lid, handle, and short spout. The teapot rim releases a thin stream of greenish liquid downward into matching bowls or cups positioned directly beneath it, suggesting freshly poured tea. Droplets fall visibly from the teapot lip into the receiving vessel. Another similar porcelain piece, possibly a covered dish or additional lidded container, appears at the lower-right edge. Behind these vessels and beside the extending wrist is a small upright teacup or bowl resting on a matching saucer atop a worn rectangular stone block. The objects are sharp compared with the background, have speckled glaze, glossy highlights, curved handles, and warm beige-gold rims.\n\nThe stone bridge surface spans horizontally and diagonally along the right foreground, with irregular paving blocks, seams, cracks, chipped corners, moss-dark crevices, and damp textures illuminated by alternating teal shadow and yellow lamp highlights. The architectural setting suggests an old canal town at night: stone arches rise behind the woman, wooden balconies cling to aged walls, hanging lamps dot the facades, and fog collects in the streets and over the water. The lighting design uses dramatic complementary color contrast—cool cyan moonlight from the sky reflects on water, jewelry, glassware, and facial contours, while orange lantern light shapes the buildings and casts warmth across the woman's shoulder, hands, and garments.\n\nThe photographic composition emphasizes intimacy and fantasy-realism: the camera is extremely close to the face and pouring tea set using wide-angle perspective, producing mild spatial distortion where the hand and utensils loom larger while the cityscape recedes dreamily behind her. Focus falloff is pronounced, with crisp detail on the woman's eyes, lips, hands, fabrics, porcelain ornamentation, droplets, and nearby stone; the background people, archways, and lanterns dissolve into bokeh-like glow. The overall mood is poetic, serene, romantic, and historically inspired, combining lifestyle portraiture, travel photography, costume styling, food-service imagery, and cinematic night scenery."
